.TH build-iso 1 "September 17, 2026" "" "CAIC"

.SH NAME
\fBbuild-iso\fR - headless ISO builder for CAIC projects

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbuild-iso\fR [\fIoptions\fR] \fIproject_directory\fR

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBbuild-iso\fR rebuilds the ISO image for an existing CAIC project without
starting the graphical wizard. It reads the project configuration
(\fIcaic.conf\fR), copies the kernel and initramfs files from the custom root
into the disk layout, builds the squashfs image, refreshes the checksum files,
recreates the attribute alias links, and rebuilds the image using the
xorriso template stored in the project.
.PP
The program is written using only the Python standard library, so it can be
run over SSH or from continuous integration. Writing to the root-owned custom
disk uses \fBpkexec\fR(1) when the command is not run as root.
.PP
With \fB--mkarchiso\fR the tool instead generates an archiso profile from the
project and delegates the build to \fBmkarchiso\fR from the archiso package.

.SH OPTIONS

\fB-h, --help\fR
.RS
show the help message and exit
.RE

\fB--mkarchiso\fR
.RS
delegate the ISO build to the \fBmkarchiso\fR tool from the archiso package,
instead of using the stored xorriso template.
.RE

\fB--work-directory\fR \fIDIR\fR
.RS
the work directory for the mkarchiso build (default:
\fI<project>/custom-temp/mkarchiso\fR).
.RE

\fB--output-directory\fR \fIDIR\fR
.RS
the output directory for the ISO (default: the project ISO directory).
.RE

\fB--skip-kernels\fR
.RS
do not copy the kernel boot files into the custom disk.
.RE

\fB--skip-squashfs\fR
.RS
do not compress the custom root file system; reuse the existing squashfs.
.RE

\fB--skip-checksums\fR
.RS
do not update the checksum files.
.RE

\fB--dry-run\fR
.RS
print the commands without running them.
.RE

.SH EXAMPLES

Rebuild a project with the stored xorriso template:

.nf
.RS
build-iso ~/caic/MyProject
.RE
.fi

Build the same project through archiso:

.nf
.RS
build-iso --mkarchiso ~/caic/MyProject
.RE
.fi

.SH SEE ALSO
\fBcaic\fR(1), \fBxorriso\fR(1), \fBmkarchiso\fR(1), \fBmksquashfs\fR(1)

